id: jf-secret-tty
title: Keep interactive setup credentials out of terminal output
description: The setup wizard must suppress terminal echo for API keys and passwords and restore input mode on completion or cancellation.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-02T18:32:37.563Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-02T18:37:17.001Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-02T18:35:38.110Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-02T18:35:38.110Z"
author: dot
acceptance_criteria: "PTY tests pass for API key, password, editing, cancellation and redirected output; required quality gates remain unchanged."
reporter: dot
severity: medium
environment: Linux PTY; Node 22.13 and 24.19; Bun 1.3.11; synthetic local fixture
repro_steps: Run the isolated setup terminal regression fixture with a synthetic credential.
resolution: Select readline terminal mode from stdin and keep secret output muted through abort and close; restore prior terminal mode in finally.
expected_result: No entered credential appears in terminal or redirected output; cancellation saves nothing.
actual_result: "Six real-PTY cases pass on Node 22.13, Node 24.19 and Bun 1.3.11. Full validate:release passed: Bun 1024 pass/185 skip, portable 1014 pass/1 skip, 9 release tests and package smoke checks. Windows PTY behavior and injected I/O failures remain untested."
